# Sources for the oil committee and proposal dispute: Painter and Brew,
# The Struggle for Iran, ch. 1; official Special Oil Commission minutes,
# first period. The recurring preparation and its effects are counterfactual.
title: Oil Committee Preparation
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: parliamentary_affairs
view-if: oil_committee_preparation_timer <= 0 and majles_convened = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; oil_committee_preparation_timer = 5

= Oil Committee Preparation

The oil dispute contains several separate questions: ownership, operations,
marketing, compensation, finance, personnel authority, and review. Committee
work can clarify those terms, build a majority around a principle, or prepare
a procedure that keeps uncertain provisions from being silently treated as
settled.

Choose what the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front's{!</span>!}
parliamentary team will make ready first.

- @oil_terms
- @oil_coalition
- @oil_record

@oil_terms
title: Compare proposal terms one by one
subtitle: Strengthen procedure while defining a minimum of national control
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 5; oil_coalition_support += 2; oil_terms_position = "Term-by-term national control"

The team creates a term-by-term comparison and leaves disputed provisions
blank rather than assigning them a neutral value. Deputies can now see whether
a proposal recognizes Iranian ownership, transfers operational authority, or
merely changes payment language.

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}'s minimum
becomes more precise and its committee case more
defensible. A careful table does not by itself create the votes to adopt it.

- @post_event: Continue

@oil_coalition
title: Build a cross-faction committee majority
subtitle: Gain direct support and improve relations with nationalist and religious allies
on-arrival: oil_coalition_support += 6; independent_nationalists_relation += 2; religious_network_relation += 2

{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} deputies meet
prospective supporters separately, asking what language
they can defend and where they will refuse compromise. {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Independent
nationalists{!</span>!} and {!<span class="term term-religious">!}religious-network{!</span>!} allies see their priorities reflected in
the effort.

The committee majority becomes more plausible. Some technical terms remain
unresolved because the work has concentrated on common ground.

- @post_event: Continue

@oil_record
title: Prepare an uncertainty register for the committee
subtitle: Strengthen procedural legitimacy and press explanation without fixing a final position
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 5; press_capacity += 3

The parliamentary team labels every provision as documented, disputed, or
still unknown and attaches the strongest available record. Friendly editors
receive the same distinctions so that uncertainty is not reported as a
compromise.

Committee work becomes more transparent and the public explanation improves.
The register deliberately stops short of selecting the final acceptable terms.

- @post_event: Continue
